1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,850
Jesus's proclamation cracked the air: "You shall be called Cephas.

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:08,012
Simon's heart pounded as the name echoed.

3
00:00:08,012 --> 00:00:13,462
What destiny lay hidden in that single utterance, and how would a simple fisherman bear it?

4
00:00:13,462 --> 00:00:18,912
What destiny lay hidden in that single utterance, and how would a simple fisherman bear it?

5
00:00:18,912 --> 00:00:27,525
Earlier that morning, Andrew had slipped away from the bustling market of Capernaum, his heart still humming from the thunder of John the Baptist’s voice.

6
00:00:27,525 --> 00:00:35,250
He had followed the whispers of a man who walked the dusty roads with a gentle authority, a man whose words seemed to bend the very air.

7
00:00:35,250 --> 00:00:44,312
When Andrew first saw Jesus standing among the hills, teaching about the kingdom, the crowd fell silent, as if the wind itself held its breath.

8
00:00:44,312 --> 00:00:50,612
Blessed are the meek,” Jesus said, his voice warm and steady, “for they shall inherit the earth.

9
00:00:50,612 --> 00:00:55,487
Andrew listened, each syllable planting a seed of awe deep within his soul.

10
00:00:55,487 --> 00:01:06,437
He had known the fire of John’s preaching, but here, under the shade of an olive tree, the fire was a steady glow that promised more than repentance—it promised a new way of living.

11
00:01:06,437 --> 00:01:12,037
Yet Andrew’s thoughts were already turning, for he could not keep this revelation to himself.

12
00:01:12,037 --> 00:01:18,075
He hurried back to his brother’s modest home by the sea, his sandals kicking up dust as he ran.

13
00:01:18,075 --> 00:01:22,825
Simon,” he called, breathless, “you must come see the Teacher.

14
00:01:22,825 --> 00:01:27,925
Simon, wiping his hands on a coarse linen, looked up from mending nets.

15
00:01:27,925 --> 00:01:32,537
Another preacher?” he asked, skepticism creasing his brow.

16
00:01:32,537 --> 00:01:35,612
He speaks of a kingdom not of this world.

17
00:01:35,612 --> 00:01:37,850
Andrew’s eyes shone.

18
00:01:37,850 --> 00:01:40,287
He is different, Simon.

19
00:01:40,287 --> 00:01:43,125
He knows things we have not yet learned.

20
00:01:43,125 --> 00:01:52,100
When they reached the place where Jesus sat among his small circle, Simon stood at the edge, watching the man whose presence seemed to calm the restless sea.

21
00:01:52,100 --> 00:01:57,037
Jesus turned his gaze upon Simon, his dark eyes meeting the fisherman’s.

22
00:01:57,037 --> 00:02:01,675
You are Simon, son of John; you shall be called Cephas.

23
00:02:01,675 --> 00:02:08,487
The name—Cephas, meaning rock—settled in Simon’s chest like a stone dropped into deep water.

24
00:02:08,487 --> 00:02:13,487
He felt the weight of it instantly, a call that trembled between fear and hope.

25
00:02:13,487 --> 00:02:17,487
Would this new name bind him to a purpose he could not yet see?

26
00:02:17,487 --> 00:02:27,487
Not far away, Philip, a thoughtful young man from Bethsaida, had been listening to the same teachings, his mind turning over each parable like a stone in a stream.

27
00:02:27,487 --> 00:02:33,437
He felt a tug, a yearning to share what he had heard with a friend whose heart was as earnest as his own.

28
00:02:33,437 --> 00:02:39,300
Nathanael,” he called, “come quickly, for you must meet the One who has stirred the heavens.

29
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:46,737
Nathanael, a man of sharp intellect and quiet confidence, walked toward them, his robe rustling against the path.

30
00:02:46,737 --> 00:02:56,400
Can anything good come out of Nazareth?” he asked, his voice edged with doubt, recalling the murmurs of the townspeople who dismissed their hometown as unremarkable.

31
00:02:56,400 --> 00:03:01,762
Jesus smiled, the corners of his mouth softening as if he had expected the question.

32
00:03:01,762 --> 00:03:06,637
Before Philip called you, when you were under the fig tree, I saw you.

33
00:03:06,637 --> 00:03:12,525
The words struck Nathanael like a flash of lightning, illuminating a hidden corner of his soul.

34
00:03:12,525 --> 00:03:21,137
He recalled the quiet moments spent under the shade of a fig tree, pondering the mysteries of the Law, never suspecting that his thoughts had been observed.

35
00:03:21,137 --> 00:03:27,075
Rabbi,” he whispered, “you are truly the Son of God; you are the King of Israel.

36
00:03:27,075 --> 00:03:33,137
The certainty in his voice startled even him, for it rose from a place deeper than mere curiosity.

37
00:03:33,137 --> 00:03:36,837
Yet the path ahead was still cloaked in uncertainty.

38
00:03:36,837 --> 00:03:41,600
How would this newfound belief shape the choices he would soon be forced to make?

39
00:03:41,764 --> 00:03:49,764
As the sun rose higher, the group gathered by a modest fire, sharing loaves and fish while the sea whispered against the shore.

40
00:03:49,714 --> 00:03:59,076
Andrew, Philip, Simon, and Nathanael listened as Jesus spoke of love, of the kingdom that would be like a mustard seed growing into a towering tree.

41
00:03:59,076 --> 00:04:05,214
The disciples felt the stir of something new, a current pulling them toward a life beyond the ordinary.

42
00:04:05,214 --> 00:04:08,339
Yet the day’s serenity hid a looming trial.

43
00:04:08,339 --> 00:04:17,664
That night, the fishermen would return to their boats, expecting the familiar emptiness of the nets, unaware that the waters held a secret that would change everything.

44
00:04:17,664 --> 00:04:23,151
What would the darkness of that night reveal, and would the fledgling followers be ready to answer?

45
00:04:23,151 --> 00:04:34,651
The conversation turned to the future, and Jesus, with a glance that seemed to pierce through time, said, “There will be a feast soon, a wedding at Cana, where I will show you what it means to trust.

46
00:04:34,651 --> 00:04:39,939
The invitation lingered in the air, a promise of a miracle that would test their faith.

47
00:04:39,939 --> 00:04:48,951
Yet before they could contemplate the feast, the shadows grew longer, and a silence settled over the sea, as if the world itself were holding its breath.

48
00:04:48,951 --> 00:04:58,764
The question hung unspoken: would the miracle that awaited them be enough to bind these men together, or would the night’s silence break the fragile thread that had just begun to form?

49
00:04:58,764 --> 00:05:08,514
The night had settled over the Sea of Galilee like a thick, sable blanket, and the moon cast a thin silver line across the water, trembling with each gentle swell.

50
00:05:08,514 --> 00:05:15,139
The fishermen’s boats bobbed in the quiet, their wooden hulls creaking softly as the tide pulled them in and out.

51
00:05:15,139 --> 00:05:23,326
Simon—who the others now called Peter—sat at the helm, his hands rough and calloused, eyes narrowed against the darkness.

52
00:05:23,326 --> 00:05:30,601
Beside him, his brother Andrew leaned forward, his shoulders hunched with the fatigue of a day spent pulling empty nets.

53
00:05:30,601 --> 00:05:40,789
James and John, the sons of Zebedee, were huddled near the prow, their faces illuminated only by the faint glow of a lantern that sputtered as if fearing the night itself.

54
00:05:40,789 --> 00:05:48,501
They had cast their nets three times already, each time pulling them up to find only the empty, frayed rope of a failed hope.

55
00:05:48,501 --> 00:05:55,914
The sea, which had been generous in other seasons, seemed to hold its breath, refusing to give them even a single fish.

56
00:05:55,914 --> 00:06:02,339
Their stomachs growled, the cold wind gnawed at their bones, and a restless unease settled among them.

57
00:06:02,339 --> 00:06:10,514
Peter’s gaze lingered on the dark horizon, where the water merged with the night, and he muttered, “Perhaps the Lord has turned His face from us.

58
00:06:10,514 --> 00:06:16,751
Just then a figure stepped onto the shore, his silhouette framed by the faint glow of a distant lantern.

59
00:06:16,751 --> 00:06:27,114
Jesus moved with a calm that seemed to belong to another world, his simple off‑white robe catching the moonlight, the red mantle draped over one shoulder flickering like a quiet flame.

60
00:06:27,114 --> 00:06:33,851
He stood a short distance from the boats, his dark eyes scanning the faces of the men who had toiled in silence.

61
00:06:33,851 --> 00:06:44,089
Put out into deep water, and let down the nets for a catch,” He said, his voice steady and clear, cutting through the night’s hush as if it were a gentle command from the wind itself.

62
00:06:44,089 --> 00:06:46,089
Peter’s heart leapt.

63
00:06:46,089 --> 00:06:51,789
The words struck a chord deeper than the ache of hunger; they were an invitation wrapped in authority.

64
00:06:51,789 --> 00:06:56,751
He turned to his brother, his eyes bright with a sudden, fierce resolve.

65
00:06:56,751 --> 00:07:04,776
Andrew, let us go out farther,” he said, his voice barely above a whisper, yet carrying the weight of an unspoken promise.

66
00:07:04,776 --> 00:07:07,026
The Master has spoken.

67
00:07:07,026 --> 00:07:11,326
Andrew nodded, his lean frame trembling with anticipation.

68
00:07:11,326 --> 00:07:19,526
The other two disciples—James and John—stood, their eyes reflecting the same fire that now burned in Peter’s chest.

69
00:07:19,526 --> 00:07:26,901
The small group moved to the side of their boat, their feet sinking into the cool sand as they pushed the vessel away from the shore.

70
00:07:26,901 --> 00:07:32,701
The oars sliced through the water, each stroke a rhythm that seemed to echo the beating of their hearts.

71
00:07:32,860 --> 00:07:39,297
When they reached the deeper part of the lake, the water grew dark and still, a mirror to the night sky.

72
00:07:39,247 --> 00:07:46,422
Peter, with a practiced hand, threw the net over the side, his movements fluid and confident despite the night’s chill.

73
00:07:46,422 --> 00:07:51,310
The rope hissed as it fell, and a moment later, the net began to fill.

74
00:07:51,310 --> 00:07:59,685
It was as if the sea itself had opened its mouth, swallowing the net and spitting out a torrent of shimmering fish that rose in a cascade of silver.

75
00:07:59,685 --> 00:08:02,447
The weight of the catch was monstrous.

76
00:08:02,447 --> 00:08:07,747
The net strained against the wooden frame, the fibers groaning under the sudden bounty.

77
00:08:07,747 --> 00:08:09,447
It’s tearing!

78
00:08:09,447 --> 00:08:13,547
James shouted, his voice a mixture of awe and alarm.

79
00:08:13,547 --> 00:08:20,447
The rope snapped in places, the net sagging and then snapping back, pulling the boat toward the water’s edge.

80
00:08:20,447 --> 00:08:28,047
The men scrambled, their muscles straining, the lantern’s light dancing across faces flushed with triumph and disbelief.

81
00:08:28,047 --> 00:08:29,497
Enough!

82
00:08:29,497 --> 00:08:34,360
Jesus called from the shore, his voice both a command and a benediction.

83
00:08:34,360 --> 00:08:38,272
Come, follow me, and I will make you fishers of men.

84
00:08:38,272 --> 00:08:43,085
Peter stared at Him, his eyes wide with a wonder that bordered on reverence.

85
00:08:43,085 --> 00:08:50,610
He could feel the pull of destiny in the tremor of his own hands, the same hands that had just hauled in a catch that would feed a village.

86
00:08:50,610 --> 00:08:53,885
Lord,” he whispered, “what must we do?

87
00:08:53,885 --> 00:09:03,610
Jesus stepped forward, his sandals leaving faint prints on the damp sand, each step deliberate, as if the ground itself recognized the significance of the moment.

88
00:09:03,610 --> 00:09:08,185
He placed a hand on Peter’s shoulder, his gaze steady and inviting.

89
00:09:08,185 --> 00:09:14,122
Leave your nets, your boats, your livelihood,” He said softly, “and come with Me.

90
00:09:14,122 --> 00:09:17,672
The harvest is not of fish, but of souls.

91
00:09:17,672 --> 00:09:22,085
The words struck a chord that resonated through every fiber of their being.

92
00:09:22,085 --> 00:09:27,910
Peter felt a surge of fear—what of his family, his trade, the life he had known?

93
00:09:27,910 --> 00:09:33,797
Yet the echo of the miracle, the abundance that had filled their nets, overpowered that fear.

94
00:09:33,797 --> 00:09:39,147
He turned to his brother, eyes shining, and said, “Andrew, we must go.

95
00:09:39,147 --> 00:09:44,147
Andrew, his lean frame now steadied by a newfound resolve, nodded.

96
00:09:44,147 --> 00:09:46,235
Yes, brother.

97
00:09:46,235 --> 00:09:48,572
The Master has called us.

98
00:09:48,572 --> 00:09:56,047
James and John exchanged glances, the younger John’s green‑tuned eyes reflecting a mixture of excitement and solemnity.

99
00:09:56,047 --> 00:10:03,897
We will follow,” James declared, his voice firm, as if sealing a pact with the very waters that had just surrendered their bounty.

100
00:10:03,897 --> 00:10:11,172
The four men moved quickly, shedding their damp cloaks, stepping onto the shore, and leaving their boats behind.

101
00:10:11,172 --> 00:10:16,922
Their footprints marked the sand, a silent testimony to a decision made in the dark hour.

102
00:10:16,922 --> 00:10:24,947
As they stood together, the sea behind them seemed to sigh, the gentle lapping of waves a soft applause to the turning of a new chapter.

103
00:10:24,947 --> 00:10:29,885
But even as they turned away from the boats, a shadow of uncertainty lingered.

104
00:10:29,885 --> 00:10:37,135
The night was still, the moon still rose, and the promise of a new path stretched before them like an uncharted sea.

105
00:10:37,135 --> 00:10:40,085
What would become of the nets they had abandoned?

106
00:10:40,085 --> 00:10:45,422
Would the miracle that had fed them be enough to sustain their faith when the road ahead grew rough?

107
00:10:45,422 --> 00:10:53,685
The first light of dawn painted the sky in soft gold as the five men gathered around the Master, their sandals dusted with the night’s sand.

108
00:10:53,685 --> 00:11:00,535
The sea’s whisper had faded, replaced by a gentle breeze that carried the scent of distant olives and wild thyme.

109
00:11:00,535 --> 00:11:06,697
Jesus turned his gaze toward the horizon, where the outline of the hills of Cana rose like a promise.

110
00:11:06,697 --> 00:11:14,097
Let us go to the wedding at Cana,” he said, his voice calm yet filled with a purpose that made the air itself seem to lean in.

111
00:11:14,260 --> 00:11:19,585
Peter felt his heart beat faster, the memory of the nets still clinging to his skin.

112
00:11:19,535 --> 00:11:27,247
Master,” he began, “the road is long, and my family—my mother, my brother—will wonder where I have gone.

113
00:11:27,247 --> 00:11:31,372
The question hung in the morning air, a knot of duty and doubt.

114
00:11:31,372 --> 00:11:34,735
Andrew placed a firm hand on Peter’s arm.

115
00:11:34,735 --> 00:11:39,722
We have already left a part of ourselves behind,” he said, his eyes steady.

116
00:11:39,722 --> 00:11:44,785
If we are to follow Him, we must trust that He knows the path for each of us.

117
00:11:44,785 --> 00:11:51,460
James, his voice low, added, “The work we have begun cannot end here; there is more to be done.

118
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:58,622
John, the youngest, looked up with bright, inquisitive eyes, as if trying to read the future in the sunrise.

119
00:11:58,622 --> 00:12:07,397
Their feet shifted on the sand, ready to step onto the road, yet a subtle unease lingered—what challenges would the journey to Cana truly bring?

120
00:12:07,397 --> 00:12:13,422
They set out, the narrow path winding between low stone walls and scattered fig trees.

121
00:12:13,422 --> 00:12:20,172
The group moved in a quiet rhythm, the soft thud of sandals against the earth punctuated by occasional murmurs.

122
00:12:20,172 --> 00:12:27,385
Philip, thoughtful as ever, fell into step beside Jesus, his mind turning over the miracle they had witnessed.

123
00:12:27,385 --> 00:12:32,485
Lord,” he asked, “do you think the people of Cana will recognize what you are?

124
00:12:32,485 --> 00:12:36,722
Jesus glanced at him, a faint smile touching his lips.

125
00:12:36,722 --> 00:12:42,672
They will see what they need to see,” he replied, “and in that seeing, they will be changed.

126
00:12:42,672 --> 00:12:54,960
The words settled like a seed in the listeners’ hearts, but a sudden rustle in the brush caught their attention—an unexpected traveler appeared, his presence stirring curiosity and a hint of apprehension among the disciples.

127
00:12:54,960 --> 00:13:01,497
As the sun climbed higher, the road opened onto a dusty village road lined with whitewashed houses.

128
00:13:01,497 --> 00:13:08,435
Children chased each other, their laughter echoing off the stone, while women carried baskets of figs and grapes.

129
00:13:08,435 --> 00:13:13,922
The group entered the town of Cana, where the scent of fresh bread rose from an open bakery.

130
00:13:13,922 --> 00:13:21,497
At the center of the town square stood a modest house, its door ajar, and a banner fluttered announcing a wedding celebration.

131
00:13:21,497 --> 00:13:27,672
The sight stirred a collective excitement; the promise of a feast and fellowship warmed their spirits.

132
00:13:27,672 --> 00:13:36,760
Yet, beneath the merriment, Jesus’ eyes scanned the crowd, lingering on a man who seemed uneasy, his shoulders hunched as if bearing a hidden sorrow.

133
00:13:36,760 --> 00:13:41,772
We are welcome,” Jesus said to the household, “and we shall share in their joy.

134
00:13:41,772 --> 00:13:48,160
The question lingered—what secret sorrow lay beneath the celebration, and how would the Master address it?

135
00:13:48,160 --> 00:13:53,335
Jesus stood at the doorway, his presence quieting the room as the murmurs faded.

136
00:13:53,335 --> 00:13:57,860
He raised his hand, and a hush fell like a blanket over the gathering.

137
00:13:57,860 --> 00:14:03,322
Let us pray,” he said, his voice resonant, inviting each heart to open.

138
00:14:03,322 --> 00:14:10,435
The guests bowed their heads, the bride’s mother clasping her hands, the groom’s father nodding in solemn reverence.

139
00:14:10,435 --> 00:14:18,597
As the prayer rose, the water in the stone jar seemed to shimmer, catching the light in a way that made the eyes of those present widen with awe.

140
00:14:18,597 --> 00:14:22,435
The Master then turned to the servants, his gaze steady.

141
00:14:22,435 --> 00:14:27,322
Fill the cups with the water,” he instructed, “and bring them to the guests.

142
00:14:27,322 --> 00:14:34,635
The servants obeyed, their movements swift, unaware that the simple act would become the first sign of something far greater.

143
00:14:34,635 --> 00:14:44,872
The moment hung in anticipation, the crowd waiting to see what would happen next—would the water become something else, and what would this mean for those who had just chosen to follow Him?

144
00:14:45,028 --> 00:14:52,965
The first cup was lifted, its contents clear and cool, and as the bride’s mother took a sip, a gasp rippled through the room.

145
00:14:52,915 --> 00:14:58,603
The liquid had turned a deep, rich crimson, its fragrance sweet as honey and wine.

146
00:14:58,603 --> 00:15:04,878
Eyes widened, whispers turned to astonishment, and the air vibrated with a new kind of wonder.

147
00:15:04,878 --> 00:15:10,365
The disciples exchanged glances, their earlier doubts dissolving like the morning mist.

148
00:15:10,365 --> 00:15:17,690
Peter felt a surge of gratitude, his earlier fears about his family now eclipsed by the magnitude of what he had witnessed.

149
00:15:17,690 --> 00:15:22,053
Lord,” he whispered, “you have shown us the power of your love.

150
00:15:22,053 --> 00:15:28,003
Jesus smiled, his eyes softening, and placed his hand on Peter’s shoulder once more.

151
00:15:28,003 --> 00:15:34,703
Your journey has just begun,” he said, “and the work of the Kingdom will be greater than any net you have ever cast.

152
00:15:34,703 --> 00:15:46,840
The celebration continued, the wine flowing, the hearts of the guests lifted, and the new disciples stood at the edge of a new chapter, their footprints now marked not only in sand but in the lives they would touch.

153
00:15:46,840 --> 00:15:51,228
Next time… we will see how Jesus turns water into wine.

154
00:15:51,228 --> 00:15:53,078
God bless you.

